    "notes": "Strat-O-Matic's own photo of the card (2019x1489, sourceImage on its som.com bucket), used in its March 2016 'SIMULATION: Goose Gossage takes on today's stars' announcement (sourceUrl). The card lies flat and square to the camera and every cell is sharp. Read twice: (1) from a 1494px view of the whole photo, (2) from 1.6x full-resolution crops of each platoon grid plus a header strip; no differences. The RHP banner text is printed very faintly on the red band: 'Power-N' is clear and a contrast-enhanced red-channel crop reads '75% AGAINST RIGHT-HAND PITCHERS' (its first digit is faint), which agrees with the LHP grid's clearly printed 25%. Markers: diamond ◆, downTriangle ▼, upTriangle △ (LHP col1 roll3 and RHP col3 roll11, each with an italic 'SI* / lo (ss)' d20 split on the two lines directly beneath; binding unambiguous), omega Ω, '?' as questionMark, underlined class letters as 'underline:C' (including the C in the LHP col2 roll8 split 'gb (2b) C 8-20'). 'plus injury' prints on its own line under HBP (col1 roll2 of both grids). Validator CHECK against his combined 2015 season (BA .0175, 1B .0324, HR .0154): this card evidently reflects only his New York Mets stint, as Strat-O-Matic cards for players traded between leagues do (its file name says 'NYM'; compare the 2017 correction for 'Addison Reed (Boston card only - 27 IP)'). Scored against the Lahman NYN stint alone (230 AB, 66 H, 14 2B, 4 3B, 17 HR, 14 BB, 54 SO, 4 HBP) every error is inside the corpus bars: BA .0114, H/PA .0107, HR .0016, BB .0089, SO .0094 (implied HR rate .068 per PA, as in 17 HR in about 250 Mets PA, vs .052 for the full season; the 4 HBP chances per grid likewise match 4 HBP in about 250 PA, not 5 in 676)."
